 'Secure Baseline':{family:'approved_security_configuration_vocabulary',qualification:'Qualify an organization-approved minimum security configuration as a configuration-management concept, not approval of this content or proof that any real system conforms.',contrasts:['A baseline is reviewed configuration guidance, while hardening is the work that reduces exposure; neither is a universal safe setting for every asset.','Approved is part of the learner definition only. Environment tailoring, change control, verification and actual owner approval remain separate and unobserved.']},
